<?jelly escape-by-default='true'?>
<j:jelly xmlns:j="jelly:core">
  <p>Works like <code>bat</code>, but additionally writes stdout/stderr to a file.</p>
  <pre>teeBat script: 'build.cmd', file: 'logs\\build.log'
def rc = teeBat(script: 'test.cmd', file: 'logs\\test.log', append: true, returnStatus: true)</pre>
  <p><code>file</code> (required, relative to the workspace), <code>append</code> (default: false).
  All other parameters are passed to <code>bat</code> unchanged.</p>
</j:jelly>
